Known product bugs behind refusals this run (not new findings - do not baseline):
  zero clock tolerance (checks.go:62): 1 refusal(s) in CLOCK-EDGE (1)
    the quorum rejects a transaction stamped even a second ahead of its own clock (core/consensus/checks.go:62, Epoch > time.Now(), whole seconds), so a sender whose clock runs a fraction of a second ahead of its quorum's is refused whenever a second ticks over between the two readings
  peer unreachable, error swallowed (ipfsport/peer.go:205): 1 refusal(s) in IPFS-RESTART (1)
    the node could not reach the other node over IPFS at all - on 2026-10-22 a node left deaf by an IPFS auto-restart, which never re-registers its p2p listener (core/ipfs_recovery.go; controller/p2p-check.sh finds them). SendJSONRequest redeclares err inside its retry loop (core/ipfsport/peer.go:205), so after every attempt fails it returns nil with an empty answer, which getPeer reads as 'the DID is not on that peer' (core/peer.go:200)

